## Problem

`erg ready`'s "claimed" abstraction is opaque — a reader sees `[claimed]` and
must investigate "by whom, when, where, how." Worse, the detection rule lives
only in source (`strings.Contains(b, id)` in ready.go), is undocumented in spec,
and has corner-case false positives (substring `0001` matches branches like
`feat/00010-foo` once IDs ever cross 9999, and more realistically slugs with
embedded digits).

Adjacent gaps:

  - **Worktrees are never mentioned in the spec.** A ticket's branch may be
    checked out in a worktree, but `erg ready` shows nothing about it.
  - **Open PRs are out of reach.** Forge probing is non-negotiably out
    (pep-erg-v1.md §7: offline + forge-agnostic). Remote-tracking branches are
    the strongest offline proxy and we already have them via `git for-each-ref
    refs/remotes`.

## Plan

### 1. Spec amendment

Add to spec-erg-v1.md, replacing the vague "looks at existing branches names"
sentence:

> A git ref **references ticket NNNN** when the literal 4-digit ID appears
> at a word boundary (start, end, or any of `/`, `-`, `_`) in its short name.
> A worktree references the ticket when its branch ref does.
>
> `erg ls` and `erg ready` annotate each open ticket with the comma-separated
> set of references found — local branch short names, remote-tracking branch
> short names (with their `<remote>/` prefix), and worktree paths. No network
> calls are made; PRs and forge issue state are out of scope
> (pep-erg-v1.md §7).

PEP §6 stays: branch *naming* is workflow, not spec. The amendment defines only
what `ls`/`ready` *recognize as a match*, which today is implicit in source.

### 2. Code changes

  - **Drop the `claimed` abstraction.** Remove `loadBranchNames`,
    `isBranchClaimed`, the `claimed` field on `readyEntry`, and the
    `[claimed]` marker.
  - **Add shared probe** in list.go: `loadRefMatches(dir, tickets)
    map[id][]string`. Runs `git for-each-ref refs/heads refs/remotes` (short
    names) and `git worktree list --porcelain`, applies the word-boundary
    matcher per ticket, returns one map. One git invocation per probe type,
    cost amortized across all tickets. Lazy gate (skip when no open tickets).
  - **Annotate in the shared printer.** Append `[ref1, ref2, ../path, ...]`
    when the set is non-empty. Same code path in `ls` and `ready`. JSON
    entries gain `refs: []string` (replaces `claimed: bool` — clean break,
    no transition).
  - **`ready` becomes a true alias.** Reduce `cmdReady` to: build the saved
    filter (`open, not blocked, not <skip-tags>`), delegate to the list
    engine, pass through `--json`. Different heading string ("Ready
    tickets"), same printer, same annotation. The branch lookup and Claimed
    section logic in ready.go disappear entirely.

### 3. UX

No `--coordination` / `--show-refs` / `-v` flag. Annotation is unconditional
when refs exist. If real usage shows it's noise, harness-log sweep can
inform a future gate; instinct is one less surface.

No `has-branch` / `has-worktree` pseudo-tag for filtering. Annotation is
greppable; `ls | grep -v '\['` is "truly unstarted." Add the pseudo-tag only
when a real need surfaces.

### 4. Forge agnostic, offline-safe

  - No `gh`, no HTTP, no `git ls-remote`.
  - Sources: `git for-each-ref refs/heads refs/remotes` (uses last-fetched
    state of remotes — stale-fetch is the user's problem, contract of
    offline tools) and `git worktree list --porcelain`.
  - No-repo / no-worktree case: probe returns empty, no annotation, no error.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Spec amendment landed in tickets/spec-erg-v1.md (matching rule + scope).
- [ ] Word-boundary matcher in code; tested for `0001` not matching
      `00010`, matching `feat/0001`, `release-0001-fixes`, `0001`, etc.
- [ ] `ls` and `ready` annotate matching local branches, remote-tracking
      branches (with remote prefix), and worktree paths.
- [ ] `ready` is a thin alias: `cmdReady` delegates to the list engine
      with the saved filter; no claimed/branch/worktree logic in ready.go.
- [ ] JSON entries have `refs: []string` (no `claimed` field).
- [ ] No network calls; tests cover offline / no-repo / no-fetch states.
- [ ] STATE.md line 29 closed out: "make erg ready an alias of erg list
      not blocking" is delivered.
- [ ] Bootstrap binary and manual refreshed.

## Non-goals

  - PR detection (out per pep-erg-v1.md §7).
  - Filtering pseudo-tags for refs/worktrees (defer).
  - Erg-managed branch naming or `erg work <id>` style helpers
    (pep-erg-v1.md §6: workflow is not spec).
